claim.claim-text:
a first node to couple to a substrate support for a substrate;
a power supply coupled to a second node, the power supply configured to provide a DC voltage to set an ion-energy at a surface of the substrate;
a first switch that couples the second node to the first node, and responsive to the first switch being closed, a first voltage is applied at the first node;
a second switch that couples a third node to the first node, and responsive to the second switch being closed, a second voltage is applied at the first node to effectuate a negative voltage at the surface of the substrate.

including
receiving a setting indicative of an energy of the ions;
adjusting the first voltage to achieve the energy of the ions.

a first node configured to couple to a substrate support for a substrate;
a power supply configured to apply a DC voltage; and
switching circuitry configured to alternately switch the DC voltage and a second voltage to the first node to effectuate a negative voltage at a surface of the substrate, which attracts ions with an ion energy to the substrate.
